      "message": "nit: Instead of adding `free` everywhere, can you use the \"goto cleanup\" style? \n\n\n```\nint ret \u003d 1;\n\nif (!s) {\n   ret \u003d 0;\n   goto cleanup;\n}\n\n...\n   \ncleanup:\n    free(copy);\n    return ret;\n```\n\nNote that it\u0027s fine to call `free(NULL)`, so this way (and the way you have written) works even when the `strdup` allocation failed.\n\nYou\u0027ll see lots of examples in the EC code if you search for usages with `git grep goto`.",
